<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Foureau–Lamy Mission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1900</span> · Also known as Foureau-Lamy Mission</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Foureau–Lamy Mission was a French military and scientific expedition of 1898–1900 led by the explorer Fernand Foureau and Commandant François Lamy. Crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> by way of Aïr and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zinder">Zinder</a>, it joined other French columns near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr">Rabih az-Zubayr</a> at Kousséri in April 1900, where Lamy was killed. It secured central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> between Algeria, the Congo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/foureau-lamy-mission.jpg" alt="Foureau–Lamy Mission" width="205" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CommandantLamy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
